Do not force -ansi.

configure.in adds "-Wall -W -pedantic -Wshadow -ansi" to CFLAGS. qcc, the
QNX compiler driver, rejects -ansi outright ("cc: -ansi no longer
supported"), so configure concludes the C compiler cannot create
executables. The same line already asks for -std=c99, which is the standard
the code is written to; drop the contradictory -ansi.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/configure.in
+++ b/configure.in
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 
 TOPDIR=`pwd`
 
-CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -DRELEASE=@RELEASE@ -Wall -W -pedantic -Wshadow -ansi -I${PWD}/CUnit/Headers -std=c99"
+CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -DRELEASE=@RELEASE@ -Wall -W -pedantic -Wshadow -I${PWD}/CUnit/Headers -std=c99"
 LDFLAGS="$LDFLAGS -L${PWD}/CUnit/Sources"
 
 AC_ARG_ENABLE(debug,
